From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Goossen <lucas.goossen@hey.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:46:31 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: clamp J313 backlight readback to the
 panel maximum

DCP 13.5 reports brightness on the old 420-nit scale after the panel
is capped at 394, so actual_brightness read back as 420 and a write of
393 came back as 419. Clamp the stored nits, and the sysfs readback,
to the panel maximum.

On this machine the panel node is read before firmware starts, so
dcp_has_panel() is already true when the backlight service is created
and answering eDP as well does not change that return. The missing
service log and the need for a modeset before writes apply are
unchanged.

Not hardware-tested.

Signed-off-by: Lucas Goossen <lucas.goossen@hey.com>
(cherry picked from commit 86a999abd1c9f430658d8882f0b13be82b43e7ae)
[j604: k610 drm sync: systemep.c conflict with upstream H17G first-report backlight registration; the clamp is applied before it, upstream lines kept.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c  |  5 +++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c | 21 ++++++++++++---------
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/systemep.c       |  7 ++++++-
 3 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
index b151887274..4eb26803bb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp_backlight.c
@@ -263,6 +263,11 @@ static int dcp_get_brightness(struct backlight_device *bd)
 		return actual;
 	}
 
+	if (dcp->brightness.nits < 0)
+		return 0;
+	if (bd->props.max_brightness > 0 &&
+	    dcp->brightness.nits > bd->props.max_brightness)
+		return bd->props.max_brightness;
 	return dcp->brightness.nits;
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
index 1e255e3ff1..5e7e486d5d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
@@ -859,7 +859,12 @@ static void iomfb_cb_pr_publish(struct apple_dcp *dcp, struct iomfb_property *pr
 			break;
 #endif
 		if (dcp_has_panel(dcp)) {
-			dcp->brightness.nits = prop->value / dcp->brightness.scale;
+			u32 nits = prop->value / dcp->brightness.scale;
+
+			/* Firmware can report the old 420-nit scale above the cap. */
+			if (dcp->brightness.maximum && nits > dcp->brightness.maximum)
+				nits = dcp->brightness.maximum;
+			dcp->brightness.nits = nits;
 			/* notify backlight device of the initial brightness */
 			if (!dcp->brightness.bl_dev && dcp->brightness.maximum > 0)
 				schedule_work(&dcp->bl_register_wq);
@@ -2802,14 +2807,12 @@ static u32 dcpep_cb_set_tiling_state_v26_6(struct apple_dcp *dcp,
 static u8 dcpep_cb_create_backlight_service(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 {
 	/*
-	 * Firmware asks during start_ios_gated, before any mode is known, but
-	 * dcp_has_panel() only becomes true once the panel dimensions have been
-	 * parsed.  13.5 does this as well as firmware 26 and newer.  An
-	 * internal panel always has a backlight, so answer for the connector;
-	 * answering false makes the firmware report that it could not find the
-	 * backlight service, and later writes are ignored until a modeset
-	 * power cycle.  connector_type is already eDP when the panel node has
-	 * been read.  External displays are not eDP.
+	 * Firmware asks during start_ios_gated. On J313 the panel node is
+	 * read first, so width_mm is already set and dcp_has_panel() is
+	 * already true. Answering eDP as well does not change this return
+	 * value. DCP 13.5 still logs that it could not find the backlight
+	 * service, and writes still apply only after a modeset.
+	 * External displays are not eDP.
 	 */
 	return dcp_has_panel(dcp) ||
 	       dcp->connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_eDP;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/systemep.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/systemep.c
index 38f667e114..f4bef95374 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/systemep.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/systemep.c
@@ -74,6 +74,7 @@ static int powerlog_report(struct apple_epic_service *service, enum epic_subtype
 	struct dcp_parse_ctx parse_ctx;
 	struct apple_dcp *dcp = service->ep->dcp;
 	int ret;
+	u32 nits;
 
 	/* Keep the existing filtering on active non-desktop backends. */
 	if (dcp_backlight_active(dcp))
@@ -119,7 +120,11 @@ have_mnits:
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	dcp->brightness.nits = mnits.millinits / 1000;
+	nits = mnits.millinits / 1000;
+	/* Firmware can report the old 420-nit scale above the cap. */
+	if (dcp->brightness.maximum && nits > dcp->brightness.maximum)
+		nits = dcp->brightness.maximum;
+	dcp->brightness.nits = nits;
 	/* H17G publishes no NITS property; its first report registers the device. */
 	if (dcp->hw.iomfb_method_profile == DCP_IOMFB_METHODS_H17G &&
 	    dcp_has_panel(dcp) && !dcp->brightness.bl_dev && dcp->brightness.maximum > 0)
